The standalone adapter replaces Navidrome/Extism types and HTTP host calls,
removes Apple Music, adds a JSON-line interface and direct metadata reader,
and deduplicates identical LRCLIB fallback queries. Provider and format code,
including KRC/YRC/QRC decoders and their upstream tests, is retained.
The Python batch runner, SSH transport, and build script are new.

Musixmatch mobile API lookup, normalization, LRC conversion and known pseudo-lyrics
rejection are adapted from navidrome-musixmatch-plugin by Myzel394 (MIT).
Upstream: https://github.com/Myzel394/navidrome-musixmatch-plugin
Reference revision: 22dc7c1e9c12ba7c900dd8abbd52c74efd9d4310.
The upstream license is reproduced in licenses/musixmatch-plugin-MIT.txt.
This adapter obtains anonymous tokens per lookup and includes no analytics,
website authentication, desktop API fallback, or token/lyrics caching.

The standalone batch tool additionally verifies identity/version metadata where
available, handles service outages separately from track rejections, and writes
optional durable JSON Lines audit reports without caching lookup results.
